## CQ-PNE-01
@group client
@commands Boot; `grep -iE "DhNoGenerationMixin\|SeasonServerConfigMixin\|SeasonBiomeConfigMixin\|SeasonColorUtilMixin\|LogSpamFilter\|Distant Horizons (dimension overrides\|refused)" logs/latest.log`
@pass no mixin apply errors, no override failure or refusal lines
@fails DH or Serene Seasons changed a target (redirect count 2, shouldDoWorldGen)
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## CQ-PNE-02
@group client
@commands Enter the Nether, fly 300+ blocks into unexplored terrain for 3 minutes; F3 DH lines; `grep -c "broken basalt columns" logs/latest.log`
@pass no LODs appear beyond the chunks actually loaded; DH world-gen threads idle; basalt warning count at most 2 (one per mod) plus the "repeats hidden" note
@fails generation not stopped in DhClientServerLevel, or filter not on the log4j context
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## CQ-PNE-03
@group client
@commands In the Nether, look over a large explored area from high up
@pass LODs end at 32 chunks; DH fog is fully thick at that edge (no hard cut against the sky or void)
@fails API override not applied (radius still 64) or fog end/max not pinned
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## CQ-PNE-04
@group client
@commands Return to the overworld; then log out and back in
@pass overworld LODs to 64 chunks and the configured fog again; `config/DistantHorizons.toml` unchanged (radius 64, fog values as before)
@fails overrides not cleared on level load / logout, or written to the file
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## CQ-PNE-05
@group client
@commands Overworld: open the world map over plains, forest, swamp, jungle, a tagged arid biome; wait for a sub-season change (or `/season set`) and look again
@pass map and block grass/foliage tints as before, and they follow the season change
@fails answers cached past a season change (they must hold per biome only; season is read live)
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## CQ-PNE-06
@group client
@commands Edit `serverconfig/sereneseasons-server.toml` blacklist (add minecraft:plains) and save while in game, F3+A
@pass plains grass loses its seasonal tint after the reload
@fails cache not cleared on Serene Seasons' ModConfigEvent
